And the Slash'Em developers fixed it by increasing the limit by 33%.

But in UnNetHack, if you ever going to hit that limit again, the
program will exit and fail and you will know how to fix it instead of
just rather silently skip the files, pretending nothing went wrong.

> So maybe my thinking has been affected by using
