You know how hard resp. annoying it is in C to do something with
dynamic memory allocation? If you don't and are used to higher-level
languages (where does stuff is mostly abstracted away from the
programmer) you can't imagine how error prone and ugly this can get.

Considering how rarely you add new level files, it's really not worth
going through the hassle of making it generic. Changing a single
constant and having the program fail is good enough in this case.

